  (text "ESP32 3V3 pin must not power these sensors (ESP32 powers nothing)." (at 160.02 243.84 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid 78acbac3-86b0-5ee3-af1c-1594402c3702))
  (rectangle (start 317.5 20.32) (end 405.13 248.92) (stroke (width 0) (type dash)) (fill (type none)) (uuid fa449271-13d8-5a24-a196-1471ecd56669))
  (text "Notes" (at 320.04 22.86 0) (effects (font (size 2.0 2.0) bold) (justify left top)) (uuid fc993a91-4b67-51c7-95b0-0f56544c7867))
  (text "1. Battery: 2S LiPo, 6.0-8.4 V (ESC LVC cuts at 6.0 V).\n   T-plug pigtail (12 AWG bare ends) soldered to J1 pads;\n   pad size TBD (footprint is the 2.5 mm2 placeholder).\n2. ESC is powered OFF-BOARD: battery -> ESC on its own\n   12 AWG leads (up to 20 A). This board carries only its\n   own loads (about 7.3 A worst case; 7.8 A at 6.0 V), so F1 is sized for\n   that, not for the motor.\n3. F1 is the single replaceable main fuse (standard ATO/ATC\n   blade in a Littelfuse FLR 178.6165 PCB holder)\n   protecting compute and both sensor rails;\n   no branch fuses.\n   Trade-off: a sensor-branch short opens F1 and drops\n   compute too (U1/U2 limit their own output current).\n   All protection values TBD.\n4. Single common GND; star point at J1 in layout.\n5. +6V_BEC is ESC-supplied (servo only), never joined\n   to a 5 V rail.\n6. Signals are 3.3 V logic or lower.\n7. U1 Pololu D36V50F5: all 12 pins drawn (2x VIN, 2x VOUT,\n   4x GND, 2x VRP, EN, PG). VRP unused (sensor buck fed\n   from VBAT). EN left unconnected: the module's\n   internal pull-up keeps it on (ESP32 EN control\n   archived). PG: open-drain, to ESP32 via J5 (ESP32\n   INPUT_PULLUP, non-strapping GPIO TBD).\n   J5 (JST-XH 6-pin) to ESP32: 1 U1_PG (GPIO TBD),\n   2 THROTTLE_PWM GPIO5, 3 STEER_PWM GPIO4,\n   4 I2C_SDA GPIO8, 5 I2C_SCL GPIO9, 6 GND.\n8. U2 EN per module datasheet (TBD); U2 footprint TBD.\n9. Rails are project power symbols (rc_power lib):\n   pin name = Value = net name.\n10. PWR_FLAG = ERC marker only (no part, not on the PCB):\n    tells ERC where power enters VBAT_RAW, GND, VBAT,\n    LDO_IN, +6V_BEC.\n11. Net classes (kicad_pro): HighCurrent = *VBAT*, GND;\n    Power5A = +5V_CPU;\n    Power3A = +5V_SENS, *+6V_BEC.\n12. J6/J7: 2-wire USB-C pigtails (20 AWG, 30 cm, about\n    0.10 V drop at 5 A; trim to 10-15 cm) into the Pi 5\n    and ESP32 USB-C inputs, keeping their own input\n    protection. Pi 5 gets no USB-PD 5 A offer (USB ports\n    limited to 600 mA unless set in config.txt).\n13. J8 Garmin LIDAR-Lite v4: 1 VIN red +5V_SENS,\n    2 GND black, 3 SDA white, 4 SCL green; I2C addr\n    0x62; no external pull-ups (13k to 3.3 V inside\n    the sensor); 3.3 V logic.\n14. Connectors: JST-XH (2.5 mm) is the convention for\n    sensors and low-power parts; exceptions J1 (battery\n    T-plug pigtail pads) and J6/J7 (USB-C pigtail\n    screw terminals, 5 A).\n15. Spec: power_board_plan.md; meeting summary:\n    design_overview.md; parts: bom.md; layout/fab:\n    fab_handoff.md. TBD values are unconfirmed." (at 320.04 30.48 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid 1a25a33d-2f88-5193-965c-ec10083f127d))
